quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  22,56,"On that Day, all sovereignty shall belong to Allah. He will judge between them. Then those who believe and perform righteous deeds shall be in Gardens of Bliss."
  22,57,"And those who disbelieve and reject Our revelations, for them shall be a humiliating punishment."
  22,58,"And those who migrated in Allah’s way, and were then slain or died, Allah shall indeed provide them with a beautiful provision. Indeed, Allah is the best of providers."
  22,59,"He will surely admit them into a place they will be well pleased with. And indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Forbearing."
  22,60,"That is so. And whoever retaliates in equal measure to what he was made to suffer and is then oppressed again, Allah will surely help him. Indeed, Allah is All-Excusing, All-Forgiving."
  22,61,"That is because Allah merges the night into the day and merges the day into the night. And indeed, Allah is All-Hearing, All-Seeing."
  22,62,"That is because it is Allah (alone) Who is the Truth, and whatever else they worship besides Him is false. And indeed, it is Allah Who is the All-Exalted, the All-Great."
  22,63,"Have you not seen that Allah sends down water from the sky so the earth becomes fresh and green? Indeed, Allah is All-Gracious All-Aware."
  22,64,"To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And indeed, Allah is the Self-Sufficient, the All-Praised."
